**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The session's item-model store reads the kit's snapshots as its other library stores do, so a kit's items resolve their models on any machine (001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine', 'missing locally → the snapshot read-only'; step 142's overlay rule; step 219: recording an item snapshots its item model). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`, after step 142's store extensions, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: `type ItemModelProxy with member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : ItemModelProxy`. `resolveItemModelVersion v` answers, for an entry the overlay's `replacements` re-bind, the held entry; otherwise the kit's snapshot of exactly that version (`LibraryEntryEnvelope.libraryVersionRef`, step 137) when the overlay holds one, so a divergent version is the kit's (001 §E); otherwise the store's. `listItemModels ()` answers the store's item models followed by the kit's snapshot-only item models, one per id at its highest version, ordered by name and then by id, a re-bound or store-held id left out (step 142's listing rule). `saveItemModel` passes through to the store. A snapshot becomes an item model only through `toItemModel` (step 210), and its refusal is `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` naming the snapshot and the refusal's `describe`. `KitLibraryStores` (step 142) is unchanged: the windows compose the overlaid item-model store beside it (step 243). No cache, write-back or other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests`: `a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library`: a kit snapshotted (step 139) from the Built-in library with the references of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` and `ItemModelIds.retarderPlateModelId` at version 1, opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder against EMPTY in-memory stores and seam (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, step 95), resolves both versions through `(ItemModelProxy .createInMemory ()).overlaidWith` of its `openOverlay []` (step 142), each equal to `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel` of its id, and `listItemModels` answers the two, by name. `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`: over the Built-in library, for a kit whose snapshot of the circular polarizer at version 1 has another description, `resolveItemModelVersion` of that version answers the kit's description, `listItemModels` answers the store's eight item models and no second circular polarizer, and `saveItemModel` of a test-local user item model through the overlaid store holds it in the underlying store. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance.

**Acceptance.** After the overlay lands, `ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith` MUST answer a kit's snapshot-only item model and the kit's copy of a divergent version, list the store's item models first and pass a save to the store; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library` and `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
